# Coin Dash: a top-down arcade game.
# Shows: no gravity, arrow-key movement, a patrolling enemy, lives, and a win and lose screen.
# Collect 10 coins. Don't let the guard catch you.

game
  size 320 by 180
  background dark slate gray

score starts at 0
lives starts at 3

thing player
  looks like gold box 10 by 10
  starts at 40, 80
  solid

thing wall
  looks like slate gray box 320 by 8
  starts at 0, 0
  starts at 0, 172
  solid
  fixed

thing guard
  looks like tomato box 12 by 12
  starts at 150, 40
  starts at 220, 130

thing coin
  looks like gold circle 3

when game starts
  set guard vx to 1.5
  make a coin at 160, 90

when left key is held
  move player left 2
when right key is held
  move player right 2
when up key is held
  move player up 2
when down key is held
  move player down 2

# Guards turn around every two seconds.
when every 2 seconds
  set guard vx to 0 - guard vx

when player touches coin
  remove the coin
  add 1 to score
  make a coin at random 20 to 300, random 20 to 150

when player touches guard
  subtract 1 from lives
  set player x to 40
  set player y to 80

when score is 10
  show text "You got them all!" in gold
  stop game

when lives is 0
  show text "Caught! Press Restart." in tomato
  stop game

always
  show text "Coins {score}   Lives {lives}" at 6, 12
